**What was denied:**
- Anything inside `../datomworld-master`, which is outside the allowed directory.
- `clojure -J-XX:StartFlightRecording=…` and `java`.
- Two ways of copying the v1 code into this repo: `git worktree add` and `git archive master`.

**What I found:**
- **v1 benchmark:** `src/clj/yin/vm/bytecode_bench.clj` on `master`. Its `:bench` alias already runs it, and it has a `--semantic-only` flag.
- **v2 benchmark:** `test/bench/yin_vm_v2_bench.cljc`. It times both the v2 AST walker and the `:semantic` VM.
- Both use the same tail-recursive countdown and time only `vm/run`, so their average (mean) run times can be compared directly.

`clj -M:test …` was allowed. I could have added a deps.edn alias to run the benchmarks through that command, but that would get around your approval settings, so I didn't.

